      "start_seconds": 0.93,
      "end_seconds": 3.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "good morning grab a seat"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.17,
      "end_seconds": 9.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.94,
      "end_seconds": 15.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.61,
      "end_seconds": 18.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.26,
      "end_seconds": 27.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a dull ache on one side of the chest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.25,
      "end_seconds": 34.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Okay when did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.42,
      "end_seconds": 46.08,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "I'd say ten days. Actually, you know, no, closer to about four days. I've also had a dry cough, since last Tuesday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.02,
      "end_seconds": 51.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "okay give me more detail on it whatever comes to mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.15,
      "end_seconds": 68.73,
      "duration_seconds": 16.58,
      "text": "Maybe a eight out of ten on a bad day. I'd say on and off. Oh, um, and weight loss. That's been about the same, about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.63,
      "end_seconds": 73.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Have you had breathlessness building over weeks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.96,
      "end_seconds": 77.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Yes, since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.36,
      "end_seconds": 81.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Would you say mild moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.04,
      "end_seconds": 84.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.38,
      "end_seconds": 88.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.55,
      "end_seconds": 95.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "I had a caesarean for my second baby nine years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.78,
      "end_seconds": 110.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.78,
      "end_seconds": 117.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "my son has asthma. My daughter has type 1 diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.42,
      "end_seconds": 130.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.24,
      "end_seconds": 144.36,
      "duration_seconds": 12.12,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.56,
      "end_seconds": 150.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.38,
      "end_seconds": 154.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I've I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 157.62,
      "end_seconds": 165.2,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "Actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to amoxicillin before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.07,
      "end_seconds": 169.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.25,
      "end_seconds": 179.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "alright, so that's unclear i'll record what each of you said what conditions have you been treated for in the the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.99,
      "end_seconds": 184.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I've had thin bones for nearly five years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.37,
      "end_seconds": 192.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "okay I can see thin bones in your file as well let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.37,
      "end_seconds": 201.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "It's something called alen... alendronate, 70 milligrams, maybe, once a week for my bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.45,
      "end_seconds": 206.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.43,
      "end_seconds": 210.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.96,
      "end_seconds": 214.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "and fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.09,
      "end_seconds": 217.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "No fever thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.24,
      "end_seconds": 223.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "And And what about leg swelling coughing up blood or night sweats?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.93,
      "end_seconds": 229.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "no, I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.25,
      "end_seconds": 233.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "how are your bowels any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.27,
      "end_seconds": 236.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 251.12,
      "end_seconds": 260.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 24, pulse 91, SpO2 93 percent on room air. BP is 121 over 86."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.95,
      "end_seconds": 263.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.55,
      "end_seconds": 268.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.83,
      "end_seconds": 273.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.82,
      "end_seconds": 276.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.93,
      "end_seconds": 296.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "there is dullness to percussion and reduced breath sounds at the right base"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.82,
      "end_seconds": 332.54,
      "duration_seconds": 31.72,
      "text": "please sit back down. Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is a pleural effusion needing a cause. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out heart failure yet. I'm sending you for a CT scan of the chest because of pleural effusion. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I think a chest X-ray makes sense here, for breathlessness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.72,
      "end_seconds": 335.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.45,
      "end_seconds": 342.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "I'll request a pleural fluid sample, it'll help with pleural effusion"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.1,
      "end_seconds": 344.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.67,
      "end_seconds": 357.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "I am arranging an urgent chest clinic review. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.87,
      "end_seconds": 361.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "thank you, that's clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.92,
      "end_seconds": 370.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Please don't wait if the the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. Come back after the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.74,
      "end_seconds": 375.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.63,
      "end_seconds": 379.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.62,
      "end_seconds": 381.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "thank you doctor goodbye"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.69,
